 "format": "Commander",
 "name": "Nick Fury: Avengers Initiative",
 "notes": [
  "Plan: Nick costs {W}. His power-up costs {W}{U}{B}{R}{G}, or {U}{B}{R}{G} on a turn he entered. It puts two counters on him, then looks at the top seven cards. One Hero, Equipment or Vehicle goes onto the battlefield, and a double-faced card can come in already flipped. 35 of the 99 are hits, so a dig averages about 2.5 hits.",
  "Free flips: Bruce Banner arrives as The Incredible Hulk, King T'Challa as Black Panther, Jennifer Walters as The Sensational She-Hulk (opponents can't cast spells on your turn), Miles as Ultimate Spider-Man, Tony Stark as The Invincible Iron Man, plus Ghost-Spider, Amazing Spider-Man, Venom and Photon.",
  "Resetting the power-up: each new Nick object gets a fresh one, and after a blink it costs only {U}{B}{R}{G}. Quantum Entanglement blinks him at your end step and the power-up is instant speed, so you can dig right then. Ephemerate, Spaceshift, S.H.I.E.L.D. Flying Car, Silver Surfer, Photon, Lady of Light and The Mighty Thor all blink him too. Helm of the Host on Nick makes a non-legendary, hasty Nick every combat, each with its own power-up.",
  "Extra digs: Wonder Man lets each Nick activate twice. Echo copies the power-up ability, and a copy isn't an activation, so it's an extra dig for {1}. Shang-Chi, Master of Kung Fu lets Echo use it the turn it lands and makes two mana for creature abilities. Karolina Dean's WUBRG each main phase can't cast spells from hand but pays Nick's power-up in full.",
  "Mana: 36 lands with 7 that make any colour, 10 tri-lands or Thriving lands, and no fetch or shock lands (his tables' B2 line). Avengers Tower, Secluded Courtyard and Unclaimed Territory (both set to Hero) pay for the power-up, because Nick is a Hero source. Only one of each basic, so the land ramp is Farseek and Cultivate rather than Forest-only searches.",
  "Top of the library: Daredevil and Iron Lad let you look at the top card any time, Herald's Horn and Origin of the Avengers filter it, and Avengers Tower bottoms the misses in any order.",
  "Damning Verdict is close to one-sided here: Nick always has counters after a dig, and Agent Phil Coulson and Captain America, Team Leader put counters on your other Heroes. Raise the Palisade naming Hero bounces every creature except yours (Birds of Paradise is the only non-Hero).",
  "Not simulated. Prices from the Nov 12 data snapshot: about $175 for the 99 at the cheapest printings. The priciest pieces are Shang-Chi $9.84, Luxury Suite $8.48, King T'Challa $8.16, Spider-Man, Miles Morales $8.04, Flawless Maneuver $7.58, Captain Marvel, Shooting Star $7.40.",
  "Flip heroes this shares with other vault decks (buy duplicates): King T'Challa (his own deck's commander), Bruce Banner (oldest's commander), Jennifer Walters (lawyer deck), Miles Morales, Gwen Stacy, Peter Parker and Spider-Man, Miles Morales (Cosmic Spider-Man deck), Eddie Brock (Thanos & Obosh), Tony Stark (Captain America deck)."
 ],
